# Tier-3 Player (`packages/player` + `apps/player`)

`@effects/player` is the **framework-agnostic Tier-3 web runtime**. Accepts a `PublishedPipeline` (Tier-1 manifest) and an optional `SupplierConfig` (Tier-2 overrides), spins up the engine, applies overrides, streams the `publishRoot` output into a caller-provided canvas. No React, no MUI, no @xyflow/react — only `@effects/runtime` and Pixi.

`apps/player` is a tiny vite+react demo on top of the package — two file pickers (pipeline required, config optional), canvas, three buttons (Load config / Reset / Back), optional events sidebar, and **canvas hit-testing for `tapZone` nodes**. Integration acceptance test: if a `(pipeline, config)` pair renders here visually identical to the supplier's preview AND its tap zones / event emitters fire correctly, every other consumer that mounts `EffectPlayer.create({ pipeline, config, canvas })` + wires its own click handler will work.

## Why this package exists

Before the split: supplier app owned `applyOverrides.ts`, `canvas-sink.ts`, `useSupplierRuntime.ts`, `supplier-config.ts`, `exporter.ts` privately. Useful to other Tier-3 consumers but locked behind the React form-app.

After: `applyOverrides` / `canvas-sink` / `SupplierConfig` / `exporter` / `createEngine` live in `@effects/player`. `EffectPlayer` is the high-level facade bundling all of the above behind one async constructor. Supplier app keeps `useSupplierRuntime` React hook as a thin adapter around `createEngine`. A partner marketplace page imports `EffectPlayer` and is done in one async call.

